      "releaseNotes": "This update:\n\n· [Added] Support for Watch Ultra 3 49 mm screen size\n\nPrevious updates:\n\n· [Added] Support for Watch Series 10 42 mm and 46 mm screen size\n· [Added] Japanese language\n· [Added] Fixed complication size for Apple Watch Ultra 1/2\n· [Added] Danish language\n· [Added] Support for watchOS 10 smart stack \n· [Added] Day and weekday above graph in-App\n· [Fixed] Complication privacy support text on small watch versions\n· [Added] Complication for Utility and other watch faces (bottom text)\n· [Added] Complication privacy support – based on your watchOS settings the complications hides when locked or in always on mode\n· [Fixed] Empty calendar list crashed app\n· [Added] Added support for Watch Series 7\n· [Changed] Text over complication style improved (bigger graph and more text) \n· [Added] Option for text overflow in event bars\n· [Added] Option for even smaller event height\n· [Added] Option for brighter grid / texts\n· [Added] Option for choosing hours in moving mode (forecast timespan)\n· [Added] Option for choosing starting and ending hour in fixed mode\n· [Added] Option for staying today (not show the graph of next day after 4pm)\n· [Added] Option for displaying the ongoing event over the complication instead of next\n· [Added] Option for display the actual date in text over complication (good for Modular Duo Watchface)\n· [Added] Support for cancelled and unknown event status (Exchange events) (appearing lighter in event list within the App)\n· [Added] New complication style for corner which shows the actual date and count of events/reminders\n· [Changed] More overview in settings\n· [Changed] List in app shows all events of today (not only upcoming)\n· [Fixed] 3-day-view again with text\n· [Fixed] 3 and 7-day-view do not show only next day after 4 pm and past last event\n· [Fixed] French language adjustments\n· [Added] Russian language\n· [Changed] All-day events with text and moving style now also with moving text within event bar\n· [Changed] Reminder with due date shown as events not sorted correctly\n· [Added] Portuguese language\n\nAny ideas or problems? Please report!",
